## [GAP ANALYSIS] Anchor check is order-sensitive

**Severity:** LOW — false positives for legitimate translations with multiple links.

### The Problem

```java
while (matcher.find()) {
    if (englishMatcher.find() && Objects.equals(matcher.group(), englishMatcher.group())) {
```

The i-th anchor of the translation must equal the i-th anchor of English. Word order differs across languages, so a sentence with two links (e.g. the old `totpStep1` form: FreeOTP link then Google Play link) may legitimately have them swapped.

### Recommendation

Compare as multisets:

```java
List<String> allowed = new ArrayList<>();
Matcher em = ANCHOR_PATTERN.matcher(englishValue);
while (em.find()) allowed.add(em.group());
Matcher m = ANCHOR_PATTERN.matcher(value);
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
while (m.find()) {
    if (!allowed.remove(m.group())) { messages.add(...); }
    m.appendReplacement(sb, "");
}
m.appendTail(sb);
```
